WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Start with what you need to remember. I built Recalen for the things that get scattered across messages and notes. This demo library includes quick thoughts, a useful reference, and a reminder.

2
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Choose what should stay. A temporary thought expires after 72 hours. A useful reference can stay Permanent until removed. That choice sits with the capture.

3
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Add structure when it helps. I can put a reference in a folder after saving it. Organization is available without being a prerequisite for capture.

4
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Find the context again. A word I remember brings back the original reference, including its text and folder context.

5
00:00:48.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Return at the right time. A reminder entered in natural language appeared with a due time and alerts. Here I can review timing, early alerts, and repeat options.

6
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Build on a thought. Longer Notes give related ideas a place to develop. A message reference can sit beside the writing and keep its preview up to date.
